[docs/docs-check         ]   | hdl/milan/KL_pp_shadow.sv:KL_pp_shadow: RESP_BASE_P — documented in bytes, not named for it: ---- AECP response buffer, also in the integrator's main memory ------ The response an AECP command builds (up to 16 + DESC_LINE_BYTES_P = 592 bytes at the shipping geometry) is not fabric state either: held as flops it measured 5,079 FF / 3,495 LUT inside KL_aecp_engine and it was those flops the placer could not pack on a die whose 135 block-RAM tiles were 100% spoken for. Same rule as DESC_BASE_P - a COMPILE-TIME base, never a register - with ONE difference that the integrator owns: this region is WRITTEN by the processor, so it must be reserved for the processor ALONE and it must not overlap the descriptor image. Passed straight through; this wrapper adds no policy.
