[docs/docs-check         ]   | protocol-processor/hdl/acmp/KL_acmp_nvm_shadow.sv:KL_acmp_nvm_shadow: LAYOUT_VER_P — documented in BYTES, not named for it: F07.8 layout_version this shadow writes and accepts 0x02 (issue #78): the record's BYTES did not change, but the meaning of `started` did. Until #78 nothing ever set it, so every record any shipped firmware persisted carries started = 0 - and started = 0 now gates the media path. Accepting those records on upgrade would fast- connect a binding that reports bound, reserves bandwidth, answers GET_STREAM_INFO with STREAMING_WAIT set, and plays nothing until a controller happens to send START_STREAMING. Refusing them costs one re-bind and cannot be silent.
